<article class="env-lemma" id="0AXY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AXY">Lemma <span data-tag="0AXY">31.11.10</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian integral scheme with generic point $\eta $. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a nonzero coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is torsion free, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\eta $ is the only associated prime of $\mathcal{F}$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\eta $ is in the support of $\mathcal{F}$ and $\mathcal{F}$ has property $(S_1)$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\eta $ is in the support of $\mathcal{F}$ and $\mathcal{F}$ has no embedded associated prime. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a translation of More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AUV" data-tag="0AUV">15.22.8</a> into the language of schemes. We omit the translation. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>